# This VM

{% if sandbar_vm_name | default('') %}
- VM name: `{{ sandbar_vm_name }}`. Host-side `sand` commands take this
  name, which can differ from `hostname`.
{% else %}
- VM name: not recorded when this VM was provisioned. Ask the user, or try
  `hostname`, which matches the name unless a custom hostname was set.
{% endif %}
{% if sandbar_profile_type | default('') %}
- Connection profile type: `{{ sandbar_profile_type }}`.
{% else %}
- Connection profile type: not recorded. A `/mnt/lima-cidata` directory
  suggests Lima (`local` or `remote-ssh`); ask the user which.
{% endif %}

Profile types:

- `local`: Lima on the user's workstation. Guest ports appear on the
  workstation's `localhost`.
- `remote-ssh`: Lima on another machine the workstation reaches over SSH.
  Guest ports appear on that machine's loopback, not the workstation's.
- `proxmox`: a Proxmox VE VM with its own network address.

See [ports.md](ports.md) for what each means for reaching a guest server.
